In article <33B8422E.50B6@itron.com>, David Bentzen <Dave.Bentzen@itron.com> writes:

>I have an Alpha 1000 4/266 machine and I want to add two external 8
>gbyte scsi disks.  The operating system is version 3.2.  Am I going to
>have any difficulty with the operating system and a large disk drive?

I shouldn't think so.  People have been able to build very large volumes
with LVM and later LSM since the operating system was released.  Some of
the UFS utilities on those really early versions had 32 bit offset
problems, but those were found and fixed.  You might want to watch
cooling wherever you happen to put them.


