We have an alpha 1000 running OSF/1 DU4 with a root disk, a usr and
normally a 16 Gb usenet RAID device. Usr and news disks were mounted as
ADVFS. Recently system started to crash. We booted into single user mode
and when trying to manually mount disks the os crashed again. I
commented out the news disk and it booted ok into init 2, but when
trying to boot into init 3 it crashed again. After I tried manually
starting services from rc3.d and it crashed again at advfsd. Now I've
set it so it doesn't run advfsd, nor it tries to mount the news disk(s)
(it still crashes if i try to mount those) and it's working, but that's
not too helpful :-(
Every time we started the machine into crashing boot it crashed just
after saying 
ADVFS EXCEPTION 
and something about bs_frag_alloc: pinpg faild
panic (cpu 0): bs_frag_alloc: pinpg faild 
and afterwards (later reboots)
ftx_bfdmn_recovery:non *done* ftx record
panic (cpu 0): ftx_bfdmn_recovery:non *done* ftx record
...
Verify doesn't find anything wrong with the advfs domains

Here is also the first kern.log where it all started. Any help is most
appreciated and needed.

Jure
